----------|\n| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (artifact consumer) | E001 produces the consumable last-activity data source (a surface on the Notebook CR) that the idle-workbench report's code reads; the console report builds against it, so the epics are serial. |\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation must describe what was built; docs-authoring is blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same — documentation of the idle-workbench report is blocked by the report's implementation. |\n| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same — documentation of the stale pipeline-run report is blocked by the report's implementation. |\n| (no edge) E001 ∥ E003 | Rule 14 | Different repos and components with no shared artifacts — the stale-run report reads KFP run metadata, not notebook activity data. Parallel. |\n| (no edge) E002 ∥ E003 | Rule 15 | Same repo (console), different areas (workbench report vs. pipeline-run report), no shared data structures or API endpoints. Parallel; merge coordination is a review-time concern, not a dependency. |\n\n## Component Mapping and Passive-Component Handling\n\nCanonical component names (from `.context/rhai-components.txt`) mapped from\nthe strategy's Affected Components list:\n\n| Strategy component | Canonical component | Owning team (from architecture context) |\n|--------------------|----------------------|------------------------------------------|\n| RHOAI web console | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard |\n| Notebook controller | Notebooks | Workbenches |\n| Kubeflow Pipelines | Data Science Pipelines | RHOAI Pipelines |\n\nActive/passive classification:\n\n- **Dashboard — active.** All new report UI and CSV export code lives here;\n  generates E002 and E003.\n- **Notebooks (notebook controller) — passive, validated by a different\n  team.** The controller already tracks last activity (architecture context:\n  `notebooks.md` — \"last activity tracked per kernel through Jupyter server\n  API probes\", consumed internally by the idle culler). No culling-behavior\n  change is requested. Per the Step 2 exception, because the consuming epic\n  is owned by the RHOAI Dashboard team while the data source is owned by the\n  Workbenches team, a separate validation/exposure Implementation epic (E001)\n  is generated and owned by Workbenches. Its deliverable is a supported,\n  consumable interface to the activity data (for example surfaced on the\n  Notebook CR); the concrete exposure mechanism is an implementation decision\n  for that team.\n- **Data Science Pipelines — passive, validated as an acceptance criterion.**\n  Run completion metadata is reachable through the documented KFP v2 REST\n  API, an interface the console already consumes to surface pipeline runs\n  (`data-science-pipelines.md`). No separate cross-team validation epic is\n  needed: validation that the report reconciles with KFP run metadata is an\n  acceptance criterion on E003.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P1 | E002 | Per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from notebook-controller activity tracking; enabled by the E001 data source. |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | E003 | Stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from KFP run metadata. |\n| HLR-3 | P2 | E002, E003 | **bundled** — CSV export renders the same report data on the same report views that the P1 work builds; each export shares the data structure and UI surface of its report, so splitting it out would double-touch the same surfaces and create an artificial serialization edge. Export ships as scope of each report epic. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | E004 | Substantive documentation authoring (new doc topics on the reports and safe reclamation steps) — separate `docs-authoring` epic per the work-product-type boundary. |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n##