tivity are distinguishable from workbenches\n  with recorded activity in the exposed data.\n- The exposure does not alter existing idle-culler behavior: culling\n  continues to function with the same defaults and per-workbench overrides\n  as before.\n- The interface and its semantics are documented for consuming teams.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P1): enabling epic — provides the data source (notebook controller\n  activity tracking) that the per-project idle-workbench report in the web\n  console is built from. Inherits P1 by priority inheritance.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41662,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87724731a85baab2","agent_id":"af14097cc984e8da3","session_id":"accbcd91-65ae-42f1-87a7-23c32a932432","uuid":"3c11fb87-c1ea-48aa-ae0d-f94cc6f1b8d1","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:52:14.245Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016"}
