{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8820a48c3ee145cd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Notebook activity data source for idle-workbench reporting\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Notebook activity data source for idle-workbench reporting\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tMakes the notebook controller's existing per-workbench last-activity tracking\n34\tconsumable by platform consumers, so the RHOAI web console can build a\n35\tper-project idle-workbench report from it. The controller already tracks last\n36\tactivity per kernel through Jupyter server API probes (this is what the idle\n37\tculler uses); this epic validates that the data is readable through a\n38\tsupported interface and, where it is not, exposes it — for example on the\n39\tNotebook custom resource — without changing culling behavior.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Determine how the notebook controller records last-activity data today and\n44\t  whether consumers of the Notebook custom resource can already read it.\n45\t- Surface the per-workbench last-activity timestamp through a supported,\n46\t  documented consumer interface if it is not already readable, keeping the\n47\t  idle culler's behavior and configuration unchanged.\n48\t- Verify the activity data is correct for workbenches in mixed states:\n49\t  recently used, idle, stopped, and never used.\n50\t- Document the interface semantics for consuming teams (update cadence, and\n51\t  what a missing value means).\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given a project with workbenches in mixed states (recently used, idle,\n56\t  stopped, never used), a platform consumer can retrieve each workbench's\n57\t  last-activity timestamp through a documented interface, and the retrieved\n58\t  values reconcile with the controller's activity tracking (recently used\n59\t  workbenches show recent timestamps; idle ones show old timestamps).\n60\t- Workbenches with no recorded activity are distinguishable from workbenches\n61\t  with recorded activity in the exposed data.\n62\t- The exposure does not alter existing idle-culler behavior: culling\n63\t  continues to function with the same defaults and per-workbench overrides\n64\t  as before.\n65\t- The interface and its semantics are documented for consuming teams.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P1): enabling epic — provides the data source (notebook controller\n70\t  activity tracking) that the per-project idle-workbench report in the web\n71\t  console is built from. Inherits P1 by priority inheritance.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b96e559e4074efe0","agent_id":"abc16d25dd159bf8f","session_id":"accbcd91-65ae-42f1-87a7-23c32a932432","uuid":"8f5c66d2-a676-4f4c-a185-1283b297557f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:54:12.397Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8820a48c3ee145cd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
