{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98a424aca6b6e86a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E002\n3\ttitle: Per-project idle-workbench report in the web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 8\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Per-project idle-workbench report in the web console\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tAdds a per-project idle-workbench report to the RHOAI web console. For each\n35\tworkbench in a project, the report shows last activity, owner, and reserved\n36\tresources, sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking, so\n37\tadministrators can see which workbenches are sitting idle and reclaim\n38\tcapacity with confidence. Includes CSV export of the report for\n39\tadministrators.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- New report view in the console, scoped per project, listing each workbench\n44\t  with its last activity (from the notebook controller's activity data),\n45\t  owner, and reserved resources, presented so administrators can identify\n46\t  idle workbenches.\n47\t- Owner and reserved resources are read from the Notebook custom resources;\n48\t  last activity comes from the consumable notebook-controller activity data\n49\t  source.\n50\t- CSV export of the report: administrators can download the report contents\n51\t  as a CSV file.\n52\t- The report is read-only — no reclamation or deletion action is offered\n53\t  (automated reclamation is out of scope for the strategy).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Given a project containing workbenches, the console shows an\n58\t  idle-workbench report listing each workbench's last activity, owner, and\n59\t  reserved resources.\n60\t- Report contents reconcile with the underlying data: owner and reserved\n61\t  resources match the Notebook custom resources, and last activity matches\n62\t  the notebook controller's activity data source.\n63\t- Given the report, an administrator can export it as CSV; the exported file\n64\t  contains the same rows and columns as the displayed report and opens in\n65\t  standard spreadsheet tooling.\n66\t- The report offers no automated reclamation or deletion action, consistent\n67\t  with the strategy's out-of-scope list.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-1 (P1): fully covered — per-project idle-workbench report (last\n72\t  activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from the notebook controller's\n73\t  activity tracking.\n74\t- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of this report is bundled into this epic\n75\t  rather than split out — the export renders the same report data on the same\n76\t  report view this epic builds, so splitting it would double-touch the same\n77\t  UI surface and data structure.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b96e559e4074efe0","agent_id":"abc16d25dd159bf8f","session_id":"accbcd91-65ae-42f1-87a7-23c32a932432","uuid":"0bce8506-97e1-415c-859b-740e5369f63e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:54:13.072Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98a424aca6b6e86a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
