\t- CSV export usage for both reports.\n53\t- Safe reclamation steps: documented manual cleanup guidance for idle\n54\t  workbenches and stale pipeline runs/artifacts, consistent with the\n55\t  strategy's out-of-scope boundary (no automated reclamation or deletion, no\n56\t  cost/chargeback calculations).\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Documentation explains both reports and their data columns, and the\n61\t  described behavior matches the implemented console reports.\n62\t- Documentation explains how to configure the stale-run age threshold and\n63\t  how to export either report as CSV.\n64\t- Documentation includes safe manual reclamation steps for idle workbenches\n65\t  and stale pipeline runs, clearly framed as manual actions with appropriate\n66\t  cautions.\n67\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented reports by the\n68\t  engineering team before publication.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-4 (P2): fully covered — documentation explains the reports and safe\n73\t  reclamation steps.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b96e559e4074efe0","agent_id":"abc16d25dd159bf8f","session_id":"accbcd91-65ae-42f1-87a7-23c32a932432","uuid":"80d2751d-2888-4f8d-b2b4-29d289ddc76c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:54:18.429Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-85596982fe57c81a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
